+- `beforeSession` is inside the `try` block, so a throw there reaches the `catch`/`finally` blocks, firing both `onError` and `afterSession`, where a deployer can assume no tools were run and the turn was aborted before provider interaction ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+- `afterSession` must tolerate partial initialization: a failing `beforeSession` may already have allocated resources, and cleanup runs before the original startup error reaches the caller when the error and cleanup hooks complete normally ([validated by: cleans up a partially initialized turn before rejecting with the startup error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.startup.test.ts#L7)).
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
